<urn:beads-cache:finding:FTQ-011> triage:id "FTQ-011" ; triage:sprint "c-1" ; triage:severity "Important" ; triage:status "open" ; triage:source "QA8 /root/c1_flaky5 and independently reproduced /root/c1_rustqa6" ; triage:record "{\"evidence\": \"process_ids:227-228 caps every inventory invocation at min(caller deadline,now+50ms), including preflight/diagnostic enumeration. Inventory::finish:190-197 kills/reaps then returns TimedOut; drain and cleanup retain that error even if subsequent cleanup succeeds. qa-7/startup-postpush-lifecycle.log records first stalled-worker case completed at5.139028833s, then owned session inventory timed out and lifecycle_supervisor_kills_and_reaps_stalled_join_families FAILED; final14passed/1failed. qa-7/startup-postpush-stalled-family-recheck.log later passes. Retained original failure copied unchanged to qa-8/flaky-retained-lifecycle-failure.log. Exact slow invocation, process state and scheduler delay were not logged, so their precise cause/phase is not asserted.\", \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-sync/tests/common/session_fixture.rs\", \"id\": \"FTQ-011\", \"issue\": \"The fixture makes successful teardown depend on a separately scheduled host-wide /bin/ps child exiting within 50 ms, independently of the enclosing 250 ms/one-second cleanup and five-second fixture budgets. Ordinary user-space scheduling or host inventory cost can therefore turn a correct lifecycle into an inventory TimedOut failure. The retained exact-head post-push suite actually failed 14/15 with that error in the stalled-join family, while the later focused family run passed. This is a concrete intermittent helper failure; unchanged helper bytes and rerunning to green do not cure it.\", \"line\": 227, \"mechanism\": \"timing_assertion\", \"recommendation\": \"Redesign inventory acquisition so test success does not depend on an individually scheduled host-wide command meeting an ambient 50 ms speed condition. Prefer a deterministic kernel/session inventory interface scoped to owned processes, retaining one hard absolute cleanup lifetime and explicit ownership/reap of any subprocess. Keep the stopped-inventory failure proof separate from healthy lifecycle assertions. Do not mask the observed failure with retries, sleep padding, suppressed timeout errors or widened lifecycle budgets.\", \"severity\": \"important\", \"test\": \"lifecycle_supervisor_kills_and_reaps_stalled_join_families and other SessionFixture users\"}" .

<urn:beads-cache:finding:FTQ-011> triage:qa8HelperCorrection "{\"evidence\": \"Original developer14/15 and independentRust13/15 retained; native inventory5/5 lifecycle18/18 store5/5 strictClippy/fmt pass after explicit slot grant; 50ms mutant fails as intended; original budgets/one attempt preserved; no self-QA closure\", \"finding\": \"FTQ-011\", \"implementation_state\": \"implemented_locally_validated_pending_postpush_proof_and_independent_QA9\", \"qa_pass\": \"C1-QA8-helper-correction\", \"receipt\": \"docs/plans/phase-c/sprint-c-1-runtime-migration.md#qa8-inventory-budget-correction-ftq-011\", \"review\": \"https://github.com/randlee/beads-cache/pull/108#issuecomment-6622741614\", \"status\": \"open\"}" .

